# What the source distribution carries, beyond the package itself.
#
# `tests/` is pruned rather than scrubbed. It is a test suite for this
# repository, not something an installer needs — and it carries the things a
# test suite legitimately carries and a published artifact should not: a
# company's product name in a fixture, and real ticket numbers from the
# project this was built against. Excluding it settles both at once.
#
# Checked, not assumed: `python -m build` put 19 test files in the sdist before
# this file existed.
prune tests
prune docs
prune extension
prune scripts
prune installer
